# rediacc_ci allowlist golden
# reader: ts:scripts/lib/blocker-validator.ts::parseBlockeredList
# command: parseBlockeredList(<corpus>, '#'); printf '%s\t%s\t%s\n' line entry blocker
# projection: records
# source: .ci-parity-exempt
# corpus: corpus/ci-parity-exempt.list
# comment-char: #
# corpus-sha256: b1a9532ca7ffd92c36cceb19c4ac5c9731afe5e91bf68d11f529dd2c96bfb48e
# ---
28	ci-only	reads the PR head/base refs from the GITHUB_* event environment; outside a pull_request event there is no branch pair to validate, so a local run has nothing to check
31	ci-only	fetches the PR's commit list over the GitHub API to assert no commit carries an unwanted Claude attribution trailer; a local checkout has no PR number and the commits are not yet pushed
34	ci-only	asks the GitHub API which account it resolves each commit's author and committer email to; that answer exists only for commits that are pushed and attached to a PR, so a local checkout has nothing to judge
37	ci-only	reads the pull request body and its updatedAt timestamp through the GitHub API to enforce the description-freshness rule; there is no PR body to read before the PR exists
40	ci-only	walks the PR's review threads via the GitHub GraphQL API and fails on unresolved ones; nothing about it is computable from a local working tree
43	ci-only	pulls bot review comments for the PR over the GitHub API and asserts each has a substantive reply; requires an open PR plus an authenticated token
46	ci-only	fetches the PR's issue-comment timeline over the GitHub API to find the newest finished review report and its reply; there is no report to answer before the PR exists and the review has run
49	ci-only	compares each submodule pointer against the branches open on the submodule's own GitHub remote; needs API access to three repos and a PR context to resolve the expected branch
52	ci-only	probes the release-state sentinels in the R2 bucket, so it needs CLOUDFLARE_R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID/CLOUDFLARE_R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY; a developer without release credentials gets "Required environment variable 'CLOUDFLARE_R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID' is not set" rather than a verdict
